{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", with an edge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{i, n + p}"},{"type":"text","text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it loses nothing."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Edges-swift.struct","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/IncidentEdgeIndices","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Neighbors"]},{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/init(base:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/base","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edgeCount","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edgeIndexBound","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edges-swift.property","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertexCount","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertexIndexBound","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertices"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/contains(_:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/contains(edge:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/degree(of:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/degree(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edgeIndex(of:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/incidentEdgeIndices(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/incidentEdges(of:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/incidentEdges(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/neighborIndices(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/neighbors(of:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/oppositeVertex(to:acrossEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertex(atIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertexIndex(of:)"]},{"title":"Type Aliases","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/IncidentEdges","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/NeighborIndices","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Vertex"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Graph-Implementations"]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges."}]},{"text":" Edge position ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"text":" is incidence number ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index order, and within a hyperedge in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices"},{"text":" order. So ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)"},{"text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array must be rebuilt for it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The LabeledGraph law.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Every index member reads the base’s rows:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shifted by n, and of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is ","type":"text"},{"code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". So ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traversal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Connectivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ShortestPaths","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the rest run on the view without hashing a vertex. ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withIncidentIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes the view’s rows out once per call from the base’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withIncidenceRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(n + m + p), so whole-graph algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices) run at an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adjacency-list copy’s speed on every base.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Costs."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a range, O(1). On ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which stores its incidences,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every read is O(1) plus the row. On any other base, ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"binary-search the hyperedge and find the member by its rank (","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" finds its place in each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over them on a base without a faster ","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberRank","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraph, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"text":" gives the bipartite structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the view’s components restricted to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"text":" are the hypergraph’s.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView.swift#L50","fileName":"IncidenceGraphView.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs18IncidenceGraphViewV","title":"IncidenceGraphView"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView/edgeIndexBound":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeIndexBound","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edgeIndexBound","title":"edgeIndexBound","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview\/edgeindexbound"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","type":"topic","title":"Graph","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between them. Kept apart from ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one, and n